<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Wampanoag Confederacy</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1676 CE (approx.) · capital Sowams</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The alliance of Algonquian communities in south-eastern New England whose sachem Massasoit befriended the Plymouth Pilgrims and whose son Metacom led King Philip's War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Wampanoag, People of the First Light, lived in some 60 or more communities across south-eastern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-massachusetts-bay">Massachusetts</a>, eastern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rhode">Rhode</a> Island, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-cod">Cape Cod</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marthas-vineyard">Martha's Vineyard</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nantucket">Nantucket</a>. A devastating epidemic in 1616 to 1619 killed a large share of them shortly before the Pilgrims arrived, and the sachem <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massasoit">Massasoit</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sowams">Sowams</a>, held the communities together.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Local sachems governed their own villages but owed loyalty to the paramount sachem, who could call councils and warriors. People farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a> and fished seasonally along the coast. In 1621 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massasoit">Massasoit</a> made an alliance with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/plymouth-colony">Plymouth Colony</a>, aided by the interpreter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisquantum">Tisquantum</a>, and shared the harvest feast later called the first Thanksgiving. Missionaries such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-eliot-missionary">John Eliot</a> founded praying towns, and the Bible was printed in Wampanoag in 1663.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>English land hunger and pressure on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massasoit">Massasoit's</a> sons <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wamsutta">Wamsutta</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metacom">Metacom</a> led to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-philips-war">King Philip's War</a> in 1675. Metacom was killed in 1676 and many captives were sold into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mashpee-wampanoag-tribe">Mashpee</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wampanoag-tribe-of-gay-head-aquinnah">Aquinnah Wampanoag</a> survive.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1600 CE – 1676 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">North America and Oceania</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.54%;width:1.51%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1676 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sowams</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Massasoit, Wamsutta, Metacom</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Algonquian traditional religion, Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Massachusett</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pokanoket, Wampanoag</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1638&amp;focus=wampanoag-confederacy" aria-label="Wampanoag Confederacy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2290 776 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Wampanoag Confederacy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3282 940h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2610 1032h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M2610 1032h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United States. <a href="/atlas?year=1638&amp;foc